in sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   in this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  the results of immunohistochemical staining for progesterone receptor protein are for investigational use only  they must not be used for clinical purposes  added by  dennis sgroi  m d  signed on  05 may 94 at 11 22 gross description  the specimen comprises two portions  the first portion represents a right modified radical mastectomy specimen displaying a completely healed 2 5cm scar  the tissue posterior to the scar looks mottled yellow  white  and gray  and it feels firm  no cavity or mass remains in this region  posterior to this location one finds two nodules  the deepest appears irregular  ill defined  and yellow and white  it spans removed_date x removed_date x 0 8cm and extends no closer than 1cm to the deep margin  slightly anterior to this nodule one finds a well defined  lobulated mass of soft  granular  red and tan tissue that has dimensions of removed_date x removed_date x 0 8cm and extends to about 2cm from the margin of the specimen  the remainder of the parenchyma looks unremarkable  section code  o   p deepest nodule q   t tissue adjacent to deep margin and deep nodule u   v more superficial nodule w  aa region of prior biopsy bb hh axillary tissue resident  frederick carl koerner  m d                                                                                  source care unit  mgh inpatient  flr unknown  reports to  carlos fernandez del castillo  m d  janey pratt  m d  irene kuter  m d  part a  right breast and axillary lymph 